Electrical, Optical, and Magnetic Properties of Materials — MIT 3.23 (@mat-mit-functional: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_3TPN5CK13R844S7PGFK7C1STVN
Nicola Marzari and David Paul, MIT, Fall 2007, graduate course. [Lecture index](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-23-electrical-optical-and-magnetic-properties-of-materials-fall-2007/pages/lecture-notes/), [assignments](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-23-electrical-optical-and-magnetic-properties-of-materials-fall-2007/pages/assignments/).

Work all available electronic and optical lectures and public problems, using the full Simon and Tong readings when slides omit derivations. The index explicitly lacks magnetic lectures 19–23. Ralph and Cambridge supply that continuation. Index labels, PDF filenames and internal lecture titles do not always align; identify readings by actual topic and content.

The inspected Bloch/reciprocal-lattice PDF has ten pages; the optical-coefficients/oscillator PDF has sixteen. Selected contents show commercial-textbook dependencies and removed or separately credited images. The public assignment index was inspected, not every solution or activity. MIT OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms have component exceptions. External reference access is distinct from permission to copy every image or the required commercial textbooks.

